#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# arg_max

#% text
# `arg_max(f, x)` gives a point where `f` attains its global maximum.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is the point of `maximize(f, x)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A downward parabola:

#% cell
arg_max(4*x - x^2, x)
#% output
#= 2

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# On an interval:

#% cell
arg_max([x^3 - 3*x, -2 <= x and x <= 3], x)
#% output
#= 3

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `maximize` gives the value too:

#% cell
maximize(4*x - x^2, x)
#% output
#= [4, [x -> 2]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `maximize`, `arg_min`, `max_value`
